  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ForumCiv: Networks Against Silence 2022-2025</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ForumCiv: Networks Against Silence 2022-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective of the Program Networks against silence: less censorship, better journalism, more democracy, is to Strengthen Latin American civil society organizations and the ecosystem of media and investigative journalists committed to the defense of freedom of expression and against censorship, the agenda of democratic inclusion, the fight against censorship and disinformation, and respect for human rights, through the promotion of regional networking and increased access to tools, resources, technical capabilities and strategic knowledge.

To achieve this objective the consortium has established two (2) components, that also translate into the outcomes of the results framework:

Outcome 1: Latin American civil society has an effective and positive impact on the expansion of freedom of expression through capacity building for the protection of journalists and the fight against censorship with a regional approach, based on the proven experience of the FLIP model.

Outcome 2: Latin America&apos;s active citizenry has an ecosystem of investigative media strengthened and committed to the defense of human rights, gender equity and equality, environmental and climate justice and inclusive democracy.

In this sense, the expected impact of the program is to contribute to a more equitable Latin American region, respectful of Human Rights and the consolidation of inclusive democracy that protects freedom of expression and promotes an enabling environment for journalism and active civil society, with full inclusion of women in their diversity and marginalized populations.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bidraget kommer att st&#xf6;dja ForumCiv, en svensk medlemsbaserad civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisation som arbetar globalt och som bildades 1995 genom en sammanslagning av tv&#xe5; paraplyorganisationer: Svensk Volont&#xe4;rsamverkan (SVS) och Bist&#xe5;ndsinformation f&#xf6;r frivilligorganisationer (BIFO). Idag har ForumCiv cirka 183 medlemsorganisationer som alla arbetar f&#xf6;r en r&#xe4;ttvis och h&#xe5;llbar v&#xe4;rld i mer &#xe4;n 70 l&#xe4;nder f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka det civila samh&#xe4;llet.

Genom ForumCiv kommer bidraget att direkt st&#xf6;dja ett konsortium av akt&#xf6;rer inom ekosystemet f&#xf6;r pressfrihet och journalistik i den latinamerikanska regionen, n&#xe4;mligen Latin American Center for Investigative Journalism (CLIP), Foundation for Freedom of Press (FLIP) och Reportrar utan gr&#xe4;nser - Sveriges internationella sektion (RSF), f&#xf6;r att utveckla ett program med titeln &quot;N&#xe4;tverk mot tystnad: mindre censur, b&#xe4;ttre journalistik, mer demokrati&quot;.

Sida kommer att st&#xf6;dja programmet med en global budget p&#xe5; 28 miljoner kronor och huvudm&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att st&#xe4;rka latinamerikanska civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer samt ekosystemet av medier och unders&#xf6;kande journalister som engagerar sig f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rsvaret av yttrandefriheten, agendan f&#xf6;r demokratisk inkludering, kampen mot censur och desinformation samt respekten f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter. Detta genom att fr&#xe4;mja regionalt n&#xe4;tverkande och &#xf6;kad tillg&#xe5;ng till verktyg, resurser, teknisk kapacitet och strategisk kunskap.

Detta bidrag &#xe4;r uppdelat i tv&#xe5; delar:

Allians mot censur: F&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkning av latinamerikanska organisationer f&#xf6;r pressfrihet och medborgarutrymme i Latinamerika samt V&#xe4;stindien, genomf&#xf6;rs av FLIP och RSR.

Resultat: Det latinamerikanska civila samh&#xe4;llet p&#xe5;verkar effektivt och positivt utvidgningen av yttrandefriheten genom kapacitetsuppbyggnad f&#xf6;r skydd av journalister samt kamp mot censur med en regional ansats, utifr&#xe5;n den bepr&#xf6;vade erfarenheten av FLIP-modellen.

Mot ett st&#xe4;rkt ekosystem f&#xf6;r unders&#xf6;kande journalistik f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;lla makten till svars i Latinamerika, genomf&#xf6;rs av CLIP.

Resultat: Latinamerikas aktiva medborgarskap har ett ekosystem av unders&#xf6;kande medier som &#xe4;r st&#xe4;rkt och engagerat i f&#xf6;rsvaret av m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter, j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och j&#xe4;mlikhet mellan k&#xf6;nen, milj&#xf6;- och klimatr&#xe4;ttvisa och inkluderande demokrati.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This contribution will support ForumCiv a Swedish member-based civil society organization that works globally, formed in 1995 by the merger of two umbrella organizations: Svensk Volont&#xe4;rsamverkan (SVS) and Bist&#xe5;ndsinformation f&#xf6;r frivilligorganisationer (BIFO). Today ForumCiv has around 183 member organizations, all working for a just and sustainable world in more than 70 countries to strengthen civil society.

Through ForumCiv, the contribution will directly support a consortium of actors, within the freedom of press and journalism ecosystem in the Latin-American region, namely, the Latin American Center for Investigative Journalism (CLIP), the Foundation for Freedom of Press (FLIP) and Reporters Without Borders &#x2013; Swedish International Section (RSF) to develop of program entitled &#x201c;Networks against silence: less censorship, better journalism, more democracy&#x201d;.

Sida will support the Program with a global budget of 28 million SEK and the main objective of strengthening Latin American civil society organizations and the ecosystem of media and investigative journalists committed to the defense of freedom of expression, the agenda of democratic inclusion, the fight against censorship and disinformation, and respect for human rights, through the promotion of regional networking and increased access to tools, resources, technical capabilities, and strategic knowledge.

This contribution is divided into two components:

Alliance against censorship: Strengthening Latin American organizations for press freedom and civic space in Latin America and the Caribbean, implemented by FLIP and RSR.

Outcome: Latin American civil society effectively and positively influences the expansion of freedom of expression through capacity building for the protection of journalists and the fight against censorship with a regional approach, from the proven experience of the FLIP model.

Towards a strengthened investigative journalism ecosystem to hold power accountable in Latin America, implemented by CLIP.

Outcome: Latin American active citizenship has an ecosystem of investigative media strengthened and committed to the defense of human rights, gender equity and equality, environmental and climate justice and inclusive democracy.</narrative>
  </description>
